# SDD pending-review marker (per-machine runtime state) + its atomic-write temps
# + the advisory-lock backing file (created by pending_review.py's _marker_lock).
# Ignore the FILES, not the .sdd/ dir — .sdd/architecture.json stays tracked.
/.sdd/pending-review.json
/.sdd/pending-review.lock
/.sdd/*.tmp

# Panel-review findings scratch (per-run working state written by the panel
# loop; author-side, never shipped). Ignore the dir, not all of .sdd/.
/.sdd/panel-findings/

# SDD working artifacts — author-side specs/design/tasks, NOT part of the
# shipped plugin (the plugin is telescoping-sdd/). Do not ship.
/specs/
/blueprint/

# Author-side working notes and evaluation records. Listed EXPLICITLY rather than
# by wildcard, so a new root-level doc is never silently ignored.
#
# ⚠️ Several of these quote internals of a private downstream project (the
# `residents` / oakleigh site) used for dogfooding — V2_24_1_REVIEW.md and
# PROMPT-EVAL-RESULTS.md in particular. This repo is PUBLIC. Ignoring them here
# so a `git add -A` cannot stage them.
/WORKING-NOTES.md
/MULTI-TYPE.md
/VERBOSITY-REVIEW.md
/V2_24_1_REVIEW.md
/OPUS5-PROMPTING-REVIEW.md
/PROMPT-EVAL-RESULTS.md
# NOT ignored, deliberately: PROMPT-EVAL-METHOD.md — written subject-agnostic
# (it names no private project) so it can be committed as maintainer docs. Left
# visible so that stays an explicit choice rather than an accident.
